: ["Newest usable poll is 52 days old; polling uncertainty inflated.", "Open seat: Steve Cohen (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Steve Cohen's retirement leaves this Memphis-area seat open, and redistricting reshaped it into a Republican-leaning district that now includes Williamson County. The partisan index favors Republicans by nine points, and every major race rating published in October calls the seat a Republican flip, ranging from Likely to Safe.\n\nDemocrat Justin Pearson has raised more money than Republican Brent Taylor, roughly four million dollars to under three million, and a Democratic-sponsored September poll showed Taylor ahead by only four points. But that survey is the only public polling, it is now seven weeks old, and prediction markets give Pearson roughly a one-in-five chance. Taylor also draws most of the outside spending recorded in the race. The evidence points to a Republican pickup, with Pearson needing a substantial late shift in turnout or persuasion to close the gap.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1065, "margin": -7.68}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.132, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1308, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.1301, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1022, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0793, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0958, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.1016, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.1226, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0978, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.1113, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.129, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.1645, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.1022, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.1028, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.1611, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.1108, "margin": -8.0